From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] network: Forget asks first, no Airplane Mode, other security
 as a page

Plinius, three changes on the Wi-Fi pages:

- Saved Wi-Fi Networks: the trash button of a network asks "Forget
  <name>?" (Cancel, Forget in red) and only then deletes it, at once.
  Before, one tap hid the row and the network was deleted when the
  "Undo" toast went away, easily missed on a phone.
- No "Airplane Mode" switch on the Wi-Fi page: airplane mode is a quick
  setting of phosh and only switched there. The page still shows
  "Airplane Mode On" while it is on and points to the quick settings,
  with a hardware switch it says to turn that off instead.
- Connect to Hidden Networks: "Other Security" (WEP, LEAP, Dynamic WEP,
  WPA & WPA2 / WPA3 Enterprise) is a page of cc-plinius-hidden-wifi.c
  (a whole file copied in prepare()) in the list style, pushed on top
  of the first page. libnma's dialog was opened in place of the first
  page, which closed itself for it, so back from there led past it to
  Wi-Fi. The libnma fallback for hidden networks goes.
---
